Given a directed graph, we want to find the shortest path between from all vertices to every other vertex. The runtime is O(n^3)

for (k = 0; k < n; ++k) {
  for (i = 0; i < n; ++i) {
    for (j = 0; j < n; ++j) {
    	A[i][j] = min(A[i][j], A[i][k] + A[k][j]);
    }
  }
}

Essentially each iteration of the outermost loop "k" is asking what is the distance between points i and j when going through the vertex pointed at by k.

